Mckissick supports Richard M. Nixon and joins the Republican Party. Mckissick isn't seen as heroic, but that doesn't mean he's not important. Sundata thinks that even though Mckissick was not a conservative Republican, he's still a less appealing character to scholars who are interested in the more radical ideals generally associated with black power. So he gets written out of the history. Mckissick is fairly well known and loved in North Carolina. And Doris says Sol City has had far reaching impacts on the state.

